			}]
		}
		{
			x: 10.0d
			y: 2.0d
			description: [
				"And we finally here. It was quick is it?"
				""
				"Patterns are the base of the autocrafting. And autocrafting is good. Because you dont need manually smelt all those ingots, craft extact amount of molten resource or smth else. It is very helpful in any modpack"
				""
				"So, how do I use that? Very simple:"
				""
				"1.Craft some blank patterns and put them into your pattern grid"
				""
				"2. Choose your recipe using jei or manually set every detail for it"
				""
				"3. Then you need some crafters. If you have refular recipe (not processing) you just placing crafter, connect it to the network and put pattern in it."
				""
				"3.5 If you have a processing pattern, things got very interesting. Place your crafter on the input side of the machine you want to automate. As example will be furnace. Side with grid and blue dot must look on that input side. Furnace got it inputside on the top, so you need to place your crafter so it look to the top side of the furnace. Then you need to supply your furnace with coal, you need exporter that will look into middle side of the furnace and filter exporter to output (for example) coal. Then you need to take items from your furnace and importer will help you with that. Place it to the output side of the machine, for furnace it will downside. And only then if you place your pattern in crafter it will work"
				""
				"3.5.5 You can craft wrench from RS to rotate crafters"
				""
				"4. Order craft from your system and it should be working just fine"
			]
			dependencies: ["49F2DD4347596082"]
			id: "5753AE2BFA43E997"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "334A88995FEDF10D"
					type: "item"
